===== Notes =====

==== Stock firmware ====
Current version is 1.0.4, SPL source archive is here: [[https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GPL/WAX206_V1.0.4.0_Source.rar]]

Appears to be based on LEDE 17.01 and can be accessed from the device (https://192.168.1.x/cgi-bin/luci/) once the root password as be set via telnet/serial/ssh.

==== Disabling Lan Leds ====
The command "mdio" is required: ''opkg install mdio-tools''

To disable lan led's run: ''mdio mt7530-0 0:0x1f raw 0x21 0x0008''

To make it permanent write it via the web UI at System->Startup->Local Startup, or via SSH into /etc/rc.local

To restore the blinking default behavior, run: ''mdio mt7530-0 0:0x1f raw 0x21 0x000b''

Source: @dmatscheko on github: [[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/11363#issuecomment-1379660930]].

====  Enabling Telnet  ====

A few options exist for enabling telnet:

  * Using serial port: <code>
service telnet start
</code>
  * Enabling via the hidden form on the [[https://router.ip/debug_detail.htm]] page:

Being logged in on the normal web interface is required.
To enable Debug mode, enter the Browser's Web Page Inspector, search HTML for ''telnet'' and unhide the entries by changing ''style="display: none;" -> style="display"'', ''hidden -> visible''. 
A checkbox "Enable Telnet" should appear in the webpage. Once clicked, the page reloads and the router can be accessed via telnet. the webUI admin account grants access to a root shell.
Set a root password to access luci at [[https://router.ip/cgi-bin/luci/]].
 
The ''debug_detail.htm'' also shows some stats like CPU/Memory/Flash Usage, one can enable Debug logging or lan/wan Packet Capturing (''.pcap'') to System Memory or USB drive. The file ''debuginfo.tar.gz'' can be downloaded directly.

  * The ''telnet-enable2.py'' tool is reported to work, see [[https://github.com/bkerler/netgear_telnet]].


